From f89f8c278a36f9c58443dada99681699a46bd2d4 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Arun Iyengar <aiyengar1990@gmail.com>
Date: Tue, 3 Nov 2026 01:52:21 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 2286/2312] media: uapi: add AVS stateless decoder pixel format
 and controls

Add a stateless decoding interface for AVS1 (GB/T 20090.2, the JiZhun
profile) and AVS+ (GY/T 257.1, the Guangdian or broadcasting profile):

- V4L2_PIX_FMT_AVS_FRAME ('AVSF'): one buffer holds one coded picture,
  its picture header and all its slices, of both fields for a field
  coded picture, with the start codes and pseudo start codes as found in
  the elementary stream. 'AVS0' and 'AVS1' are used by stateful drivers
  out of tree.
- V4L2_CID_STATELESS_AVS_SEQUENCE: the video sequence header.
- V4L2_CID_STATELESS_AVS_PICTURE: the I or P/B picture header, the
  offset of the first slice and three resolved references (forward,
  second forward and backward), each with its capture buffer timestamp,
  picture_distance, picture type and field structure, which is what
  direct and skip mode prediction need. Userspace keeps the reference
  history: only I and P pictures are references, and P pictures have
  two of them.
- V4L2_CID_STATELESS_AVS_WEIGHT_QUANT: the AVS+ weighting quantisation
  syntax elements as coded, for pictures that use it. Decoders that need
  the matrices derive them from these.

There is no slice control: the decoders this is written for parse the
slice headers themselves.

The controls are validated as the other stateless controls are: flag
masks, ranges, the required references of P and B pictures, and zeroed
reserved fields. The structures have no holes: 16, 64 and 32 bytes, with
the same layout on 32 and 64-bit ABIs.

Assisted-by: LLM
Signed-off-by: Arun Iyengar <aiyengar1990@gmail.com>
